<title>RUSSIA: AGROKHLEB-Russian sugarbeet area down 13 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>AGROKHLEB-Russian sugarbeet area down 13 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<text>
<p>The following is a direct contribution from SovEcon Ltd, an independent research organisation specialising in agricultural production and trade in the former Soviet Union.</p>
<p>ESTIMATE OF RUSSIAN SUGARBEET AREA REVISED DOWNWARDS</p>
<p>MOSCOW, June 18 - The total area sown to sugarbeets this year is estimated at about 930,000 hectares, or 12-13 percent down on last year's level (Table 1).</p>
<p>This is the lowest level since the early 1950's.</p>
<p>Delayed sowing is likely to result in reduced yields in the range of 15-17 tonnes per hectare.</p>
<p>SovEcon's forecast of total sugarbeet output in 1997 is 15-16 million tonnes (1996: 16.1 million tonnes).</p>
<p>This may be the second lowest output level in the last forty years.</p>
<p>By early June, the sugarbeet sowing campaign was nearly completed.</p>
<p>Due to a cold spring, sowing was delayed in all regions (Table 2).</p>
<p>High production costs, coupled with lower domestic demand for sugar, discouraged producers from maintaining plantings at last year's level.</p>
